  = note: use a `&'static` slice of `&'static str`, an array, a `Vec` or an iterator of texts, or a signal, memo or closure of a `Vec` of strings
  = help: the following other types implement trait `IntoOptions<M>`:
            `&'static [&'static str; N]` implements `IntoOptions<twine_view::marker::Slice>`
            `&'static [&'static str]` implements `IntoOptions<twine_view::marker::Slice>`
            `Memo<Vec<S>>` implements `IntoOptions<Reactive<S>>`
            `OptionsProp` implements `IntoOptions<twine_view::marker::Prop>`
            `ReadSignal<Vec<S>>` implements `IntoOptions<Reactive<S>>`
            `Signal<Vec<S>>` implements `IntoOptions<Reactive<S>>`
            `twine_view::Prop<Vec<S>>` implements `IntoOptions<twine_view::marker::Prop>`
